// --- An image, with no struct of its own ---
//
// An image is a horizontal box: a GtkPicture measures its height for the
// width it is given, and a vertical box gives each child its own whole
// width, so the picture asked for as much height as that width implies; a
// horizontal box measures it at its own width. What the program says of the
// image -- its fit, what runs as it is clicked, as its picture arrives and
// as it fails -- and why its last picture failed are a value C holds on it.
//
// A source is a GtkPicture, and what it says -- whether what it shows
// arrived, why not, whether the image holding it was told, and a drawing's
// size and paint -- a value held on it. The texture it shows it holds under
// "sngl-texture"; the picture it watches, the image it last told and the
// window whose icon it is are pointers it keeps and does not hold, under
// "sngl-picture", "sngl-frame" and "sngl-icon-of".
//
// A picture is a GObject of its own: what the program says of it -- its
// URL, whether it arrived and why not, how many hold it -- held on it, its
// texture held under "sngl-texture", and the sources watching it a GList
// under "sngl-watching", each taken out as it goes. Its holders share one
// reference on the object and a fetch still on its way another, so a
// picture given back before its fetch arrives goes once it does.
//
// A window's icon is a source appended to it, kept under "sngl-icon-widget"
// and pointed to under "sngl-icon": the runtime's box calls and its window
// hand these to the three functions sngl_image_hooks is handed.

